    ("NZ", "Science", MARCUS,
     "Drones help scientists track kauri dieback in Northland forests",
     "Aerial images spot sick trees before symptoms are visible from the ground.",
     [
         "Scientists in Northland are using drones fitted with special cameras to find kauri trees infected with dieback disease, sometimes years before the damage is visible from the forest floor.",
         "Kauri, among the largest and longest-lived trees in the world, are threatened by a soil-borne pathogen that has killed thousands of trees since it was identified in 2008.",
         "## How the cameras see it",
         "Infected trees take up less water, which changes the way their leaves reflect light in wavelengths the human eye cannot see. The drones fly over the canopy and capture these changes across hundreds of hectares in a day.",
         "In a trial in the Waipoua Forest, the drones identified 43 trees with early signs of infection. Ground tests confirmed the disease in 37 of them.",
         "“Walking through the forest to check trees spreads the disease on our boots,” said a forest ecologist on the project. “From the air, we can look without touching anything.”",
         "## Protecting the giants",
         "Tāne Mahuta, the largest known living kauri, stands in Waipoua.",
         "Tracks near the oldest trees have been closed or rebuilt as raised boardwalks, and visitors must clean their shoes at wash stations at track entrances. Iwi have led much of the protection work, including a rāhui closing the Waitākere Ranges near Auckland from 2018.",
         "## What happens next",
         "Researchers plan to survey all of Northland's major kauri forests by 2027. The maps will help rangers decide where to close tracks and where to test treatments, such as injections of a compound that slows the disease in infected trees.",
     ]),
